From: mscharged-port
Subject: Graphics validation leaves out the checks inside shaders
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host diagnostics. Apply after 0131.

Validation (0005) asked Dawn for its full level, which on D3D12 also turns on
the debug layer's GPU-based validation and on Metal the shader validation.
GPU-based validation patches each pipeline on its first use in a command
list: a Windows match with every pipeline made at start still stalled 0.2 to
0.8 s on the first draws, and every frame was two to three times slower. The
partial level keeps the API validation of every backend (the Vulkan layers
are the same at both levels) without the shader checks.

diff --git a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
index ba15313..b2b4518 100644
--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
@@ -801,8 +801,13 @@ bool initialize(AuroraBackend auroraBackend, bool allowCpu) {
     }};
     dawn::native::DawnInstanceDescriptor dawnInstanceDescriptor{};
     dawnInstanceDescriptor.nextInChain = &instanceTogglesDescriptor;
+    // The backend's API validation (the D3D12 debug layer, Metal's API
+    // validation, the Vulkan validation layers) without its checks inside
+    // shaders: D3D12's GPU-based validation patches each pipeline on its first
+    // draw, which stalls play although every pipeline was made at start, and
+    // it and Metal's shader validation slow every frame.
     dawnInstanceDescriptor.backendValidationLevel = g_config.enableBackendValidation
-        ? dawn::native::BackendValidationLevel::Full
+        ? dawn::native::BackendValidationLevel::Partial
         : dawn::native::BackendValidationLevel::Disabled;
     dawnInstanceDescriptor.SetLoggingCallback(wgpu_log);
     dawnInstanceDescriptor.platform = dawn_platform();
